      "text": [
        "Fixture Bank Limited — Data Governance Charter — Template",
        "Powered by DGIW",
        "ILLUSTRATIVE",
        "What this document is",
        "This is the charter TEMPLATE, rendered because the active engagement has no actionable intake. Every page carries the",
        "ILLUSTRATIVE watermark and the provenance log records mode: reference. Nothing in it is client-specific, and nothing in it",
        "should be presented as such. Fill the Program Design intake — organisation name, at least one driver, at least one pillar in",
        "scope — and regenerate to produce the engagement version.",
        "What each section will contain",
        "Mandate",
        "The organisation, its sector, and the primary driver the programme answers — from the intake’s",
        "organisation and drivers sections.",
        "Drivers",
        "The regulatory and strategic drivers, as the engagement names them — from the intake’s driver",
        "lists.",
        "Scope and explicit exclusions",
        "Which of the eleven pillars are in scope, and — explicitly — which are not. Exclusions are stated,",
        "never implied by absence.",
        "Sponsorship and governance",
        "The executive sponsor and council chair role titles, the council cadence and the escalation path —",
        "from the intake’s sponsorship section. The full council terms of reference remain the operating",
        "model’s (AR-09).",
        "Decision rights and accountability",
        "The engagement’s own RACI rows — activities with at least one assignment. Rows never filled in",
        "are never printed.",
        "Approval",
        "The sponsor’s role title with signature and date slots. Slots stay blank until signed on paper — this",
        "workbench never fabricates a signature or a date.",
        "Authored per engagement, outside the intake",
        "A signed charter also carries the following. No intake field captures them yet, so they are named here rather than silently omitted or padded with",
